# WIN-OODAC FEASIBILITY — Phase 0 research, sub-agent C

File: openOODA/audit/win_oodac_feasibility.oot
Date: 2026-08-19. Lane: read-only. Sub-agent: C of 4.
Tool note: this Explore session has read, glob, grep only. No bash, no file, no stat. All file sizes, ELF magic, and bytes are inferred from scripts and docs, not directly observed.

## 0. Scope and finding summary
- Read ooda/oodac/main.oo, ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build, ooda/bootstrap/seed/README.oot and SIGNING.oot, ooda/runtime/chs_rt.c (umbrella), and the full chs_rt_*.c set.
- The compiler is pure .oo. It has zero host-header includes and zero extern "C" declarations. The Linux-only surface is in the C runtime and in three sh invocations in oodac/*.oo.
- The seed binary at ooda/bootstrap/seed/oodac is gitignored and not present on this host (only signing artifacts). A working tree rebuild is the everyday path.
- Recommendation: a Windows oodac.exe is feasible. The .oo compiler source is portable. The chs_rt_*.c runtime needs a Windows shim layer; the bash build script must be replaced with a mingw-aware driver.

